From c69ae0d911cbd2f6394b935a320f09aa490acd7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sepp <biondogs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:38:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL HOTFIX (t_c58c5eed): one-shot chat -q died host-wide on
 inherited automation source labels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kanban dispatcher (and cron/a2a) sets HERMES_SESSION_SOURCE, which the
terminal tool bridges into every child process. GatewaySessionStore.create()
sent that label verbatim as session.create's `source`; the canonical create
contract (tui_gateway/contracts/canonical_sessions.py, Literal over SURFACES)
refuses non-surface labels with a bare 4001 invalid_params (no field/detail,
logged nowhere at INFO), so every `hermes chat -q` run from a worker terminal
died at agent init with "couldn't start the model connection: invalid_params".
The thin client (gateway_chat) never inherited the label, which is why only
the classic CLI one-shot path broke.

Fix: GatewaySessionStore.gateway_source() keeps main's label inside the
surfaces the gateway advertises via runtime.describe — an inherited
non-surface label falls back to the thin client's own rule (oneshot for a
finite run, cli otherwise); an explicit --source the gateway cannot serve
raises the thin client's "does not support source" copy instead of the
opaque refusal. Older gateways (describe without sources) keep the old
pass-through behavior.

Patch copy: /local/projects/software-co/patches/chat-oneshot-source-local.patch
Rollback anchor = pre-patch HEAD fe5e8bd91a.

Agent-Profile: sw-dev-a
Agent-Run: t_c58c5eed
